{"content_hash": "f2f1785871bc8ced", "version_id": 594, "article_id": 60, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "Indonesia frees eight orangutans after Borneo wildfires", "title_zh": "婆罗洲大火后，印尼放归八只红毛猩猩", "has_translation": true, "topic": "science", "source": "bbc_science", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/videos/c6073z5rvrk3o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1586778538929-ee34a8e9d8e7?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Mnx8d2F0Y2glMjBlbmRhbmdlcmVkJTIwb3Jhbmd1dGFuc3xlbnwwfDB8fHwxNzkxNzY1NzczfDA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Dan Dennis on Unsplash", "author": "Dan Dennis", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@cameramandan83?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/brown-monkey-on-brown-wooden-log-during-daytime-5ESfIy0yjZY?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(180, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(218, 46%, 48%)", "label": "SCIENCE", "seed": "459c4da79085"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-12", "word_count": 203, "reading_minutes": 1.0, "lead": "Eight critically endangered orangutans have been returned to the wild in Borneo. They were among 46 rescued by Indonesian wildlife authorities when fires destroyed their habitat last year.", "lead_zh": "八只极度濒危的红毛猩猩已在婆罗洲被放归野外。去年大火摧毁它们的栖息地时，印尼野生动物部门共救出46只，它们正是其中一部分。", "preview": "Eight orangutans have been released into the wild in Borneo after being rescued from intense wildfires, according to Indonesian wildlife aut", "preview_zh": "据印尼野生动物部门消息，八只红毛猩猩在从猛烈野火中获救后，已被放归婆罗洲野外。这批猩猩于周五在该岛西部的一个保护区被释放，包括三只母猩猩、它们的三个女儿和两只成年公猩猩。红毛猩猩属于极度濒危物种。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 583, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/60/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 77.288, "size_bytes": 467424, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 225, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@4c59139/content/data/versions/594.json", "paragraphs": ["Eight orangutans have been released into the wild in Borneo after being rescued from intense wildfires, according to Indonesian wildlife authorities. The group, which was freed on Friday in a reserve in the west of the island, included three mothers, their three daughters and two adult males. The apes are critically endangered.", "Before the fires tore through their habitat in August and September, officials had rescued 46 of the animals. The operation was carried out by Indonesian wildlife teams, who moved the apes to safety as the flames spread. Without such action, experts say, many more of these rare creatures would have died.", "The release marks an important step for conservation in the region. Orangutans are native to Borneo and Sumatra, and their numbers have fallen sharply because of habitat loss, farming and fires. Each successful return to the wild is seen as a small victory for those working to protect the species.", "Wildlife groups warn that rescue efforts alone cannot save the orangutans. They argue that stronger protection of forests is needed to prevent future fires and to secure a long-term home for the animals. The eight released this week will be monitored as they adapt to life back in the wild."], "paragraphs_zh": ["据印尼野生动物部门消息，八只红毛猩猩在从猛烈野火中获救后，已被放归婆罗洲野外。这批猩猩于周五在该岛西部的一个保护区被释放，包括三只母猩猩、它们的三个女儿和两只成年公猩猩。红毛猩猩属于极度濒危物种。", "在去年八九月大火席卷它们的栖息地之前，官员们已救出46只红毛猩猩。这次行动由印尼野生动物团队执行，他们在火势蔓延时将猩猩转移到安全地带。专家表示，如果没有这样的行动，会有更多这种珍稀动物死亡。", "此次放归标志着该地区保护工作迈出重要一步。红毛猩猩原产于婆罗洲和苏门答腊，由于栖息地丧失、农业开发和火灾，其数量已急剧下降。每一次成功回归野外，都被视为保护该物种工作的一次小胜利。", "野生动物组织警告说，仅靠救援行动无法拯救红毛猩猩。他们认为，需要加强对森林的保护，以防止未来发生火灾，并为这些动物确保长期的家园。本周放归的八只猩猩将在适应野外生活的过程中受到监测。"], "body": "Eight orangutans have been released into the wild in Borneo after being rescued from intense wildfires, according to Indonesian wildlife authorities. The group, which was freed on Friday in a reserve in the west of the island, included three mothers, their three daughters and two adult males. The apes are critically endangered.\n\nBefore the fires tore through their habitat in August and September, officials had rescued 46 of the animals. The operation was carried out by Indonesian wildlife teams, who moved the apes to safety as the flames spread. Without such action, experts say, many more of these rare creatures would have died.\n\nThe release marks an important step for conservation in the region. Orangutans are native to Borneo and Sumatra, and their numbers have fallen sharply because of habitat loss, farming and fires. Each successful return to the wild is seen as a small victory for those working to protect the species.\n\nWildlife groups warn that rescue efforts alone cannot save the orangutans. They argue that stronger protection of forests is needed to prevent future fires and to secure a long-term home for the animals. The eight released this week will be monitored as they adapt to life back in the wild.", "body_zh": "据印尼野生动物部门消息，八只红毛猩猩在从猛烈野火中获救后，已被放归婆罗洲野外。这批猩猩于周五在该岛西部的一个保护区被释放，包括三只母猩猩、它们的三个女儿和两只成年公猩猩。红毛猩猩属于极度濒危物种。\n\n在去年八九月大火席卷它们的栖息地之前，官员们已救出46只红毛猩猩。这次行动由印尼野生动物团队执行，他们在火势蔓延时将猩猩转移到安全地带。专家表示，如果没有这样的行动，会有更多这种珍稀动物死亡。\n\n此次放归标志着该地区保护工作迈出重要一步。红毛猩猩原产于婆罗洲和苏门答腊，由于栖息地丧失、农业开发和火灾，其数量已急剧下降。每一次成功回归野外，都被视为保护该物种工作的一次小胜利。\n\n野生动物组织警告说，仅靠救援行动无法拯救红毛猩猩。他们认为，需要加强对森林的保护，以防止未来发生火灾，并为这些动物确保长期的家园。本周放归的八只猩猩将在适应野外生活的过程中受到监测。", "text": "Eight orangutans have been released into the wild in Borneo after being rescued from intense wildfires, according to Indonesian wildlife authorities. The group, which was freed on Friday in a reserve in the west of the island, included three mothers, their three daughters and two adult males. The apes are critically endangered. Before the fires tore through their habitat in August and September, officials had rescued 46 of the animals. The operation was carried out by Indonesian wildlife teams, who moved the apes to safety as the flames spread. Without such action, experts say, many more of these rare creatures would have died. The release marks an important step for conservation in the region. Orangutans are native to Borneo and Sumatra, and their numbers have fallen sharply because of habitat loss, farming and fires. Each successful return to the wild is seen as a small victory for those working to protect the species. Wildlife groups warn that rescue efforts alone cannot save the orangutans. They argue that stronger protection of forests is needed to prevent future fires and to secure a long-term home for the animals. The eight released this week will be monitored as they adapt to life back in the wild.", "vocab": [{"word": "endangered", "pos": "adj", "zh": "濒危的", "note": "常与 critically 连用，表示极度濒危", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "release", "pos": "verb", "zh": "释放；放归", "note": "文中指把动物放回野外", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "rescue", "pos": "verb", "zh": "营救；救援", "note": "既可作动词也可作名词", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "wildfire", "pos": "noun", "zh": "野火；山火", "note": "指难以控制的自然火灾", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "habitat", "pos": "noun", "zh": "栖息地", "note": "动物或植物自然生长的地方", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "reserve", "pos": "noun", "zh": "保护区", "note": "为保护动植物而划出的区域", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "conservation", "pos": "noun", "zh": "保护；保育", "note": "常指对自然环境的保护", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "species", "pos": "noun", "zh": "物种", "note": "单复数同形", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "native", "pos": "adj", "zh": "原产的；本土的", "note": "be native to 表示原产于某地", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "monitor", "pos": "verb", "zh": "监测；跟踪", "note": "指持续观察并记录情况", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "adapt", "pos": "verb", "zh": "适应", "note": "adapt to 表示适应新环境", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}, {"word": "long-term", "pos": "adj", "zh": "长期的", "note": "反义词为 short-term", "phonetic": "", "en": ""}], "title_original": "Watch: Endangered orangutans released back into the wild after Borneo fires", "summary_original": "The critically endangered apes were rescued from intense wildfires that destroyed their habitat in August and September.", "body_original": "Watch: Endangered orangutans released back into the wild after Borneo fires\nTo play this video you need to enable JavaScript in your browser.\nThis video can not be played\nWatch: Endangered orangutans released back into the wild after Borneo fires\nClose\nEight orangutans have been released into the wild in Borneo after being rescued from intense wildfires.\nThree mothers, their three daughters and two adult males were freed in a reserve in the west of the island on Friday.\nIndonesian wildlife authorities rescued 46 of the apes, which are critically endangered, before fires tore through their habitat in August and September.\nRead more on this story.\nSubsection\nAsia\nPublished\n50 minutes ago\nShare\nclose panel\nShare page\nCopy link\nAbout sharing\nRelated topics\nIndonesia\nFollow\nIndonesia\nclose panel\nYou are now following\nIndonesia\nUpdates from your News topics will appear in\nMy News\nand in a collection on the\nNews homepage\n.\nOrangutans\nFollow\nOrangutans\nclose panel\nYou are now following\nOrangutans\nUpdates from your News topics will appear in\nMy News\nand in a collection on the\nNews homepage\n.\nBorneo\nFollow\nBorneo\nclose panel\nYou are now following\nBorneo\nUpdates from your News topics will appear in\nMy News\nand in a collection on the\nNews homepage\n.\nConservation\nFollow\nConservation\nclose panel\nYou are now following\nConservation\nUpdates from your News topics will appear in\nMy News\nand in a collection on the\nNews homepage\n.\nWildfires\nFollow\nWildfires\nclose panel\nYou are now following\nWildfires\nUpdates from your News topics will appear in\nMy News\nand in a collection on the\nNews homepage\n.\nRead description", "fetched_at": "2026-10-12T00:42:52.124893", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Eight", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.312, "sm": 100, "